WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:07.622
OLIVIA: Hello, Little Fox readers! Welcome back to People in the News . Today we're going

2
00:00:07.623 --> 00:00:14.944
to meet Vera Wang, a famous fashion designer and very successful businesswoman. You've probably even seen

3
00:00:14.945 --> 00:00:19.608
celebrities wearing her stunning designs! BEN: That's right, Olivia. Vera is famous for her dress designs,

4
00:00:19.609 --> 00:00:26.122
especially her wedding dresses. She also created her own company and built it into a successful

5
00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:31.207
business. But she did not become a fashion designer and entrepreneur until a bit late in life—after

6
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:37.785
she turned forty. Vera was born on June 27, 1949, in New York City. Both her

7
00:00:37.786 --> 00:00:42.926
parents came from important families in China, and her father was a very successful businessman in

8
00:00:42.927 --> 00:00:51.020
the United States. Growing up in Manhattan, Vera and her family lived an affluent lifestyle. She

9
00:00:51.021 --> 00:00:56.091
attended an exclusive private school and traveled frequently with her mother to Paris, where they went

10
00:00:56.092 --> 00:01:01.510
to famous fashion designers' shows and bought custom-made clothing. These trips helped Vera to develop a

11
00:01:01.511 --> 00:01:06.920
love for fashion at an early age—and develop a sharp eye for good design. When Vera

12
00:01:06.921 --> 00:01:14.419
was eight years old, she began taking figure-skating lessons. She became very serious about competing and

13
00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.083
even designed her own skating dresses. At first her dream was to skate in the Olympics.

14
00:01:19.084 --> 00:01:25.080
But when it came time to try out for the team, she placed only fifth, narrowly

15
00:01:25.081 --> 00:01:28.816
missing her chance to go to the Olympics. OLIVIA: She must have been really disappointed. What did

16
00:01:28.817 --> 00:01:37.141
she do next? BEN: Well, she chose to give up figure skating and move to Paris

17
00:01:37.142 --> 00:01:42.219
to study art. There, Vera was reminded of her childhood love for clothing, and she decided

18
00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:47.128
to pursue a career in fashion design. But when she told her parents about her plans,

19
00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:54.470
her father wanted her to do something more practical and refused to pay for design school.

20
00:01:54.471 --> 00:02:02.287
So Vera found a different way to do what she loved. After her graduation from college,

21
00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:05.959
she took a job at Vogue, a leading fashion magazine. Vera started as an assistant at

22
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:12.028
Vogue and had to work long, hard hours—sometimes even spending the night at the office. However,

23
00:02:12.029 --> 00:02:20.180
her hard work paid off, and at the age of 23, Vera became the youngest fashion

24
00:02:20.181 --> 00:02:28.195
editor in Vogue history. Vera loved working at Vogue and stayed there for about 15 years

25
00:02:28.196 --> 00:02:34.178
as a senior editor. Next she worked for the fashion designer Ralph Lauren. She became the head

26
00:02:34.179 --> 00:02:37.761
designer for accessories, which included bags and jewelry. She loved designing and jumped up and down

27
00:02:37.762 --> 00:02:42.672
with excitement whenever she spotted someone with something that she'd designed. Vera was around forty years

28
00:02:42.673 --> 00:02:49.662
old when she and her longtime boyfriend decided to get married. As an older bride, she

29
00:02:49.663 --> 00:02:55.319
grew frustrated by the lack of options for fashionable wedding dresses. She finally gave up shopping

30
00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:01.492
for a dress and designed her own! Later, when Vera quit her job to start a

31
00:03:01.493 --> 00:03:05.895
family, her father offered to help her start her own business and suggested that she focus

32
00:03:05.896 --> 00:03:14.720
on bridal fashion. Vera wanted to design other types of clothing, but she took her father's

33
00:03:14.721 --> 00:03:22.372
suggestion and opened a bridal boutique in 1990. At first Vera sold dresses made by other

34
00:03:22.373 --> 00:03:29.300
famous designers, but soon she was designing her own wedding gowns. Vera had no formal education

35
00:03:29.301 --> 00:03:36.300
in design, but her years of working in the fashion industry had taught her a lot. She

36
00:03:36.301 --> 00:03:41.131
was very creative and put her own modern twist on everything. She also made sure that

37
00:03:41.132 --> 00:03:46.946
her designs would reflect the woman's personality and sense of style. Soon her wedding dresses grew

38
00:03:46.947 --> 00:03:52.126
very popular among brides. Vera also provided excellent service and helped brides with wedding planning. Many

39
00:03:52.127 --> 00:03:56.782
people believe that Vera transformed the bridal industry by making it more fashionable and influencing other

40
00:03:56.783 --> 00:04:05.696
designers to expand into wedding dresses. OLIVIA: Didn't she also become famous for designing figure-skating dresses?

41
00:04:05.697 --> 00:04:10.510
BEN: That's right, Olivia. When Nancy Kerrigan was competing in the 1992 and 1994 Olympics, she

42
00:04:10.511 --> 00:04:18.836
asked Vera to design her dresses. One dress, covered with thousands of crystals, sparkled as Nancy

43
00:04:18.837 --> 00:04:25.431
skated and caught everyone's attention. Even though Vera had never made it to the Olympics, her

44
00:04:25.432 --> 00:04:31.588
dresses had, making her very proud! After that Vera branched out into evening gowns, with many

45
00:04:31.589 --> 00:04:41.098
famous women such as actresses and first ladies wearing Vera Wang dresses to important events. Still Vera

46
00:04:41.099 --> 00:04:48.908
didn't want to be known just for her wedding dresses and gowns. She was determined to

47
00:04:48.909 --> 00:04:56.495
design other types of clothing. In 2004 Vera launched a collection of clothes that would be

48
00:04:56.496 --> 00:05:05.125
sold in stores instead of custom-made for individual buyers. Her collection received great reviews, and in

49
00:05:05.126 --> 00:05:08.303
2005 the Council of Fashion Designers of America awarded her with the Womenswear Designer of the

50
00:05:08.304 --> 00:05:15.213
Year, the most prestigious fashion award in the industry. At the age of 55, Vera had

51
00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:24.024
finally achieved her dream of becoming a well-established fashion designer. Today Vera's designs continue to use

52
00:05:24.025 --> 00:05:30.196
a variety of silhouettes, colors, and materials, which stand out for their boldness and creativity. In

53
00:05:30.197 --> 00:05:37.864
2012 she surprised everyone by creating a collection of red wedding dresses. Although most of Vera's

54
00:05:37.865 --> 00:05:43.521
products are very expensive, she has started lower-priced lines so that more people can wear her

55
00:05:43.522 --> 00:05:46.868
designs. She's also expanded her company to include menswear, jewelry, perfume, and china. Vera achieved her dream

56
00:05:46.869 --> 00:05:53.389
a bit late in life. But once she got started, it took her only about twenty

57
00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:57.337
years to build a multimillion dollar retail empire and become recognized as one of the world's

58
00:05:57.338 --> 00:06:04.495
leading designers. OLIVIA: Wow, that’s impressive. Thanks for telling us about Vera's success in the fashion

59
00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:09.914
industry, Ben. Maybe someday we'll get to see you wearing a Vera Wang tuxedo or suit!

60
00:06:09.915 --> 00:06:17.252
Thanks for tuning in to another edition of People in the News , Little Fox readers.

